cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Sacred GF16/TF3 findings, please cite this work. φ-optimal number formats with 98.4% information retention."
title: "Trinity B006: Sacred GF16/TF3 — Phi-Based Number Formats for Ternary Computing"
abstract: "We present Sacred GF16 and TF3, φ-optimal number formats designed for ternary neural network inference. Key innovations include: (1) GF16 format [sign:1][exp:6][mant:9] with φ-distance 0.049 (40% better than IEEE f16); (2) TF3 format: 18-bit ternary with base-3 exponent; (3) φ-distance metric |e/m - 1/φ| for optimality measurement; (4) Theorem: GF16 achieves minimal φ-distance among 16-bit formats; (5) 98.4% information retention vs FP32 baseline; (6) Round-trip error analysis with statistical confidence intervals. Mathematical foundation: Trinity Identity φ² + φ⁻² = 3 proves balanced ternary {-1, 0, +1} is natural for φ-based computing. Pure Zig implementation with conversion utilities, packing functions, and FPGA synthesis support. Complete mathematical proofs, statistical analysis, and hardware synthesis results."
